  "summary": "Healthcare AI continues advancing but faces real-world adoption challenges. Aidoc won FDA breakthrough status for its radiology report automation, while Trase secured $107 million for healthcare AI agents, and documentation tools like Abridge are expanding beyond physicians into nursing workflows. However, clinicians remain skeptical of AI despite its potential, and successful implementations require human oversight rather than full automation. Meanwhile, virtual care adoption is climbing, though many health systems struggle with profitability on digital services, and data management remains problematic as healthcare data lakes risk becoming unstructured swamps. On the policy front, Democrats are pushing legislation to cap Medicare out-of-pocket costs and reform the 340B drug discount program, while regulators are scrutinizing pharmaceutical marketing practices with antitrust investigations into Sanofi's flu vaccine campaign. The sector also faces emerging challenges including medetomidine-laced opioids causing severe withdrawal symptoms in jails and a new metabolic disease now covered by FDA-approved therapy.",
